1. Introduction
   Project Overview:
   In today's digital marketing landscape, businesses require a centralized and efficient platform
   to manage and track their advertisements. This proposal presents a Web-Based system for
   Advertising Agency that enables advert creation, management, tracking, asset storage,
   payment handling, and customer support. The system is designed for advertisers, media
   teams, and admin users to collaborate effectively, ensuring high-impact advertising
   campaigns.
   Objectives:
   ● Facilitate advert creation and scheduling in multiple formats
   ● Provide performance analytics and real-time tracking
   ● Enable centralized storage and reuse of ad assets
   ● Ensure secure role-based access and user account management
   ● Streamline invoicing and ad activation through integrated payment systems
   ● Provide robust customer support via chat and FAQs
   Target Users:
   ● Internal:
   ○ System Administrator
   ○ Marketing Manager
   ○ Graphic Designer
   ○ IT Support
   ○ Customer Support
   ○ Finance Team
   ● External:
   ○ End users/clients
   ○ Payment Gateway
   ○ Email Service
   Scope:
   ● Fully web-based application (responsive for mobile browsers)
   ● Supports static and multimedia advert formats
   ● Integrates with third-party payment APIs
   ● Application will be hosted locally for demonstration purposes
   Limitations:
   ● Browser compatibility (modern browsers only)
   ● File size limitations for uploads (max 5MB static files, 100MB video files, 50 MB audio
   files)
   ● Payment gateway integration shown as mockup/simulation
   ● Full production features will require cloud deployment
   ● No real-time multi-user testing capabilities
   ● Local database storage limitations (MySQL localhost)
   ● File uploads restricted to local machine storage
   ● No direct integration with external advertising platforms (e.g. Google Ads)
   ● Third party payment gateway availability
   ● Users have basic computer literacy
   ● Stable internet connection for real time features
